    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0305" n="299" xml:id="pg299"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 153.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Commissioner of the United States to China</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Peking, China</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1901-08-12"><hi rendition="#italic">August
                                12, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copy
                    of a note addressed by the dean of the diplomatic corps, under date of the 8th
                    instant, to the Chinese plenipotentiaries, asking the financial cooperation of
                    their government in the work of improving the navigability of the Peiho and
                    Whangpu rivers, and their acceptance of the regulations concerning the
                    organization, duties, and revenues of the Whangpu River Conservancy
                        board.<anchor n="a" xml:id="d173-f1"/></p>
                <p>The regulations will figure as an annex to the Final Protocol.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d173-a1.xml" xpointer="d173-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d173-f1" n="a" xml:id="d173-f1-content">
                <p>For regulations, see Final Protocol, annex No. 17.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
